Using polymorphing, I think your best chance is to start as a wizard with
a ring of polymorph control, and then hope to come across a sink, or
a ring or wand of polymorph. It seems every time I try just zapping the
shopkeeper with a wand of polymorph, he resists my magic, steps over to
me and kills me in about one turn. Polymorphing into a cockatrice is
guaranteed, since by default if you get hit the shopkeeper will turn to
stone. Laying eggs while in this state is handy too, particularly if you
have a ring of conflict.

Further opinions on the subject:

The easiest way to rob a shop is to become invisible and just blast away
with a suitable wand.

The safest way is to dig into the shop, then dig a trapdoor just
outside, collect everything you want, and walk out.

Now, a QUESTION: Can you have two shopkeepers on the same level?

I robbed a shop recently using the trapdoor method, and in the course of
my travels I went back to that level. Upon returning cautiously to the
scene of the crime (to retrieve some stuff which I couldn't carry), I
found that the shopkeeper was gone, and in fact was nowhere on the
level. I assume he fell in my trap door. I subsequently wandered around
the next dungeon level or two in mortal fear, afraid that he would be
lurking somewhere around on one of these levels. The thing was, though,
that there was a shop also on the next level. I never saw the shopkeeper
again, and so perhaps he fell through to the next level, but since the
game may not allow two shopkeepers on one level, he was destroyed.

COROLLARY: If the above assumption is true, then a great new method of
killing shopkeeper has just been invented. Anytime you find a shop with
another shop on the level below, (as in Peter's game), dig a trapdoor
directly in front of the shop doorway. Then dig your way in, collect
the stuff and walk out. The shopkeeper will come running out the front
door in pursuit, and fall staight down the trap door and into oblivion.

Of course, if you can have two shopkeepers on a level, I will have to
content myself with getting a wand of probing and a ring of conflict,
and stand next to them and watch as they beat each other senseless.
Prize Fight of the Century. Where's Don King when you need him!

So, can anyone shed any light on this? Does it work? Has anyone ever
tried it.

